WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:17.362
was confined to a dark and lonely room for a week after he had dared to ask for

2
00:00:17.402 --> 00:00:17.962
more gruel.

3
00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:21.825
No one responded to the notice offering him as an apprentice.

4
00:00:22.786 --> 00:00:26.788
The workhouse board began to think about sending him to sea to work as a cabin boy.

5
00:00:27.709 --> 00:00:28.970
The board members sent Mr.

6
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.372
Bumble out to make some inquiries to ship captains.

7
00:00:32.372 --> 00:00:35.994
He was just returning to the workhouse when he met the village undertaker, Mr.

8
00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:37.275
Sowerberry, at the gate.

9
00:00:37.295 --> 00:00:41.317
"I've come for the two women who died last night," said Mr.

10
00:00:41.357 --> 00:00:44.299
Sowerberry as he cordially stepped forward and shook Mr.

11
00:00:44.339 --> 00:00:44.960
Bumble's hand.

12
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.901
"You'll make a fortune when the board pays you, Mr.

13
00:00:47.941 --> 00:00:49.302
Sowerberry," said Mr.

14
00:00:49.342 --> 00:00:51.924
Bumble. The undertaker shook his head.

15
00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:56.607
"The amount paid by the board for the paupers' coffins is very small."

16
00:00:57.647 --> 00:00:58.688
"So are the coffins!"

17
00:01:00.288 --> 00:01:04.210
Mr. Bumble allowed himself only a smile because he was an important official.

18
00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:05.591
But Mr.

19
00:01:05.651 --> 00:01:09.072
Sowerberry was very amused by the joke and laughed for a long time.

20
00:01:09.093 --> 00:01:10.613
"Well, Mr.

21
00:01:10.633 --> 00:01:16.356
Bumble," he said at last, "there's no denying that the coffins are somewhat narrower since you started feeding

22
00:01:16.396 --> 00:01:17.377
the paupers less."

23
00:01:18.437 --> 00:01:20.598
That reminded the parish officer of Oliver.

24
00:01:20.618 --> 00:01:23.720
"You don't know anybody who wants an apprentice, do you?"

25
00:01:24.712 --> 00:01:28.934
Mr. Bumble raised his cane to the notice on the gate and gave three raps on the words

26
00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:30.155
"Five Pounds."

27
00:01:31.176 --> 00:01:33.377
"That's the very thing I wanted to speak to you about!

28
00:01:34.398 --> 00:01:38.300
I pay so much in taxes to support the poor, I have a right to get a lot

29
00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:38.740
out of them.

30
00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.361
So I'll take the boy myself."

31
00:01:42.362 --> 00:01:46.264
Mr. Bumble grasped the undertaker by the arm and hurried him into the workhouse.

32
00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:50.546
Within five minutes the board decided that Oliver should go to Mr.

33
00:01:50.587 --> 00:01:52.968
Sowerberry immediately for a month's trial period.

34
00:01:54.656 --> 00:01:59.240
That evening Oliver was brought before the board and informed that he was to become an apprentice to

35
00:01:59.280 --> 00:01:59.921
the undertaker.

36
00:01:59.941 --> 00:02:05.726
"And if you ever complain or come back to this workhouse again, you will be sent to sea,"

37
00:02:06.086 --> 00:02:06.486
said Mr.

38
00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.787
Limbkins, the head of the board.

39
00:02:07.807 --> 00:02:10.249
"Do you understand, boy?"

40
00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.252
Oliver nodded and showed no emotion.

41
00:02:13.272 --> 00:02:16.915
"Oh, he's a hardened young rascal," said Mr.

42
00:02:16.955 --> 00:02:19.017
Limbkins as Oliver was led away by Mr.

43
00:02:19.037 --> 00:02:22.280
Bumble. The other board members nodded in agreement.

44
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:28.244
So Oliver pulled his cap over his eyes, picked up the small brown paper parcel that contained all

45
00:02:28.284 --> 00:02:31.226
his belongings, and once more attached himself to Mr.

46
00:02:31.246 --> 00:02:32.086
Bumble's coat cuff.

47
00:02:33.127 --> 00:02:34.108
For some time Mr.

48
00:02:34.128 --> 00:02:36.309
Bumble drew Oliver along without noticing him.

49
00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:42.774
This was partly because the parish officer held his head high, as an important parish officer always should.

50
00:02:43.735 --> 00:02:45.736
And this was also because it was a windy day.

51
00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.499
Little Oliver was completely hidden by Mr.

52
00:02:49.539 --> 00:02:51.220
Bumble's coat whenever it blew open.

53
00:02:52.328 --> 00:02:54.969
As they drew near their destination, however, Mr.

54
00:02:55.009 --> 00:02:58.731
Bumble thought he should make sure that the boy was ready for inspection by the undertaker.

55
00:02:58.751 --> 00:03:00.932
"Oliver!" said Mr.

56
00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:05.113
Bumble. "Yes, sir," replied Oliver in a low, tremulous voice.

57
00:03:05.134 --> 00:03:08.655
"Pull that cap off your eyes and hold up your head."

58
00:03:09.675 --> 00:03:11.576
Oliver immediately did what he was told.

59
00:03:12.557 --> 00:03:15.338
As he was pushing up his cap, a tear fell on his hand.

60
00:03:16.258 --> 00:03:16.778
And as Mr.

61
00:03:16.818 --> 00:03:20.220
Bumble gazed sternly upon him, another tear rolled down his cheek.

62
00:03:21.192 --> 00:03:23.153
It was followed by another and another.

63
00:03:24.253 --> 00:03:26.894
Oliver covered his face with both hands and wept.

64
00:03:27.855 --> 00:03:29.235
Mr. Bumble glared at Oliver.

65
00:03:29.255 --> 00:03:35.858
"Well, of all the most ungrateful and worst-behaved boys that I have ever seen, Oliver, you are the—"

66
00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:38.599
"No, no, sir."

67
00:03:38.979 --> 00:03:39.699
Oliver sobbed.

68
00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.400
"I will be good.

69
00:03:42.381 --> 00:03:43.381
Indeed, sir, I will.

70
00:03:44.361 --> 00:03:48.983
I'm a very little boy, sir, and it's so so "So what?"

71
00:03:49.343 --> 00:03:50.844
Mr. Bumble asked in amazement.

72
00:03:51.888 --> 00:03:52.869
"So lonely, sir.

73
00:03:53.889 --> 00:03:54.890
So very lonely!

74
00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:56.851
Everybody hates me.

75
00:03:57.852 --> 00:03:59.413
Oh, please don't be angry with me!"

76
00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:01.334
For a moment Mr.

77
00:04:01.354 --> 00:04:03.535
Bumble regarded Oliver with some astonishment.

78
00:04:04.495 --> 00:04:10.379
"Ahem well, yes ahem oh, this troublesome cough," said the parish officer.

79
00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:14.541
He cleared his throat and managed to keep the tears from his own eyes.

80
00:04:14.561 --> 00:04:18.804
"Now dry your eyes and be a good boy," he finally said to Oliver.

81
00:04:19.796 --> 00:04:22.317
He took Oliver's hand and they walked on in silence.

82
00:04:23.378 --> 00:04:27.340
Mr. Sowerberry was busy making some entries in a ledger when they arrived at his shop.

83
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.002
"Here!" said Mr.

84
00:04:30.022 --> 00:04:32.103
Bumble. "I've brought the boy."

85
00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:33.864
Oliver made a bow.

86
00:04:33.884 --> 00:04:36.245
"Oh, that's the boy, is it?"

87
00:04:37.185 --> 00:04:39.967
The undertaker raised his candle to get a better view of Oliver.

88
00:04:39.987 --> 00:04:44.289
"Mrs. Sowerberry, will you have the goodness to come here a moment, my dear?"

89
00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.991
Mrs. Sowerberry emerged from a little room behind the shop.

90
00:04:48.011 --> 00:04:50.264
"My dear," said Mr.

91
00:04:50.304 --> 00:04:53.506
Sowerberry, "this is the boy from the workhouse that I told you about."

92
00:04:54.507 --> 00:04:55.347
Oliver bowed again.

93
00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.068
"Oh, my!"

94
00:04:57.569 --> 00:04:58.689
said the undertaker's wife.

95
00:04:58.709 --> 00:05:00.790
"He's very small."

96
00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.892
"Yes, he is rather small," agreed Mr.

97
00:05:03.932 --> 00:05:05.853
Bumble. "But he'll grow."

98
00:05:05.873 --> 00:05:10.956
"I daresay he will grow, once he starts eating our food and drink," said Mrs.

99
00:05:10.996 --> 00:05:17.280
Sowerberry. "I see no saving in employing workhouse children for they always cost more than they're worth.

100
00:05:18.304 --> 00:05:20.245
But men always think they know best.

101
00:05:21.226 --> 00:05:23.287
Get downstairs, little bag of bones."

102
00:05:24.248 --> 00:05:25.069
With that, Mrs.

103
00:05:25.129 --> 00:05:29.532
Sowerberry opened a door and pushed Oliver down a steep flight of stairs to the kitchen.

104
00:05:30.532 --> 00:05:34.915
A servant girl was sitting in the kitchen, which was a damp, dark room just outside the cellar.

105
00:05:34.935 --> 00:05:37.437
"Here, Charlotte," said Mrs.

106
00:05:37.477 --> 00:05:39.738
Sowerberry, who had followed Oliver downstairs.

107
00:05:39.758 --> 00:05:43.781
"Give this boy the cold meat scraps you were saving for the dog.

108
00:05:44.722 --> 00:05:47.944
That animal hasn't come home all day, so he'll have to do without.

109
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.082
I'm sure this boy isn't too fussy to eat them.

110
00:05:52.122 --> 00:05:52.723
Are you, boy?"

111
00:05:53.703 --> 00:05:55.725
Oliver's eyes lit up at the mention of meat.

112
00:05:56.786 --> 00:05:57.506
"Oh no, ma'am."

113
00:05:58.547 --> 00:06:02.630
Charlotte set a plate of meat scraps before him, and Oliver gobbled up the dog's food.

114
00:06:04.231 --> 00:06:05.572
In silent horror Mrs.

115
00:06:05.612 --> 00:06:07.253
Sowerberry watched Oliver eat.

116
00:06:08.254 --> 00:06:11.536
If he was this hungry now, how much would he eat when he was bigger?

117
00:06:11.556 --> 00:06:15.139
"Well," she said when Oliver had finished his supper.

118
00:06:15.159 --> 00:06:16.820
"Are you done?"

119
00:06:17.936 --> 00:06:19.237
Oliver looked around the kitchen.

120
00:06:20.158 --> 00:06:22.039
There was nothing more to eat within his reach.

121
00:06:22.059 --> 00:06:24.321
"Yes," he said.

122
00:06:24.341 --> 00:06:26.182
"Then come with me."

123
00:06:27.103 --> 00:06:30.665
Mrs. Sowerberry picked up a dim and dirty lamp and led the way upstairs.

124
00:06:30.685 --> 00:06:33.027
"Your bed's under the counter.

125
00:06:33.927 --> 00:06:35.789
You don't mind sleeping among the coffins?"

126
00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.350
Oliver hesitated on the stairs.

127
00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:44.254
"Well, it doesn't matter whether you do or don't because you can't sleep anywhere else," said Mrs.

128
00:06:44.294 --> 00:06:46.216
Sowerberry. "Come on!

129
00:06:46.592 --> 00:06:47.874
Don't keep me here all night!"

130
00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:51.699
Oliver meekly followed his new mistress upstairs.
